rule ROUTE107 "handler-returns-exception-text" {
  lang python
  severity error

  find fn: function where fn.text ~ /return\s+(str|repr)\(\s*(e|ex|exc|err|error|exception)\s*\)/
  report fn "a handler returns the text of a caught exception to the client"

  example fire python """
    def view():  #~ error
        try:
            return work()
        except Exception as e:
            return str(e), 500
  """
  example clean python """
    def view():
        try:
            return work()
        except Exception:
            log.exception("work failed")
            return "internal error", 500
  """
  example notapplicable markdown """
    Prose returns nothing.
  """
  explain """
    The text of an exception names files, queries and library internals. Returning it to the client leaks them. The check reads `return str(e)` and `return repr(e)` by text inside any Python function; other languages and frameworks need an adapter and are reported Unresolved by the family, never clean.
    ## Remedy
    Log the exception server side and return a generic message with an error id.
  """
}
